# Build output at the repo root. The leading slash is load-bearing: a bare
# `aiauth` also matches the SOURCE DIRECTORY cmd/aiauth/, hiding every file in
# it from `git add`. cmd/aiauth/main.go is tracked and stays tracked whatever
# this file says, so nothing was lost — but the next file added beside it would
# have been skipped in silence.
/aiauth
logs/
.inber/
